1
00:02:30,005 --> 00:02:35,825
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:36,145 --> 00:02:40,165
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,405 --> 00:02:44,365
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,985 --> 00:02:49,225
Hunky D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,525 --> 00:02:51,985
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,365 --> 00:02:54,965
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,265 --> 00:02:58,085
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:58,085 --> 00:03:01,165
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,145 --> 00:03:03,885
Stop this sight!

10
00:03:04,905 --> 00:03:07,725
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,425 --> 00:03:11,505
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,725 --> 00:03:15,665
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,645 --> 00:03:24,565
After being separated from his crew, Luffy set out to rescue his captured brother Ace.

14
00:03:24,565 --> 00:03:28,085
To do so, he snuck into the government prison, impelled down.

15
00:03:28,865 --> 00:03:32,025
Bon Clay, who was saved by Ivankov of New Karma Land,

16
00:03:32,365 --> 00:03:37,185
has just learned that Luffy's treatment against Warden Magellan's deadly poison has already begun.

17
00:03:37,285 --> 00:03:39,645
Making miracles is never easy!

18
00:03:42,385 --> 00:03:43,885
Believe in miracles!

19
00:03:44,305 --> 00:03:46,145
Bon Clay's cries from the heart!

20
00:03:46,145 --> 00:03:57,825
Miracle!

21
00:03:58,825 --> 00:03:59,965
Nothing less.

22
00:04:00,745 --> 00:04:04,205
And even then, it'll take a tremendous one for Straw Hat Boy to survive.

23
00:04:04,325 --> 00:04:06,825
After everything he's been through, he's in rough shape.

24
00:04:06,905 --> 00:04:09,645
You said it takes courage and spirit to make a miracle work,

25
00:04:09,725 --> 00:04:10,965
and Straw Boy's got both!

26
00:04:10,965 --> 00:04:14,585
I know he can do it!

27
00:04:14,765 --> 00:04:15,785
He can do anything!

28
00:04:16,245 --> 00:04:18,325
That's why I'm not nervous in the least!

29
00:04:18,625 --> 00:04:21,005
Then practice what you preach and take a deep breath.

30
00:04:21,185 --> 00:04:23,145
All we can do is wait and trust in him.

31
00:04:23,145 --> 00:04:24,145
Uh-huh.

32
00:04:27,145 --> 00:04:33,785
I ate the horn horn fruit!

33
00:04:34,205 --> 00:04:37,925
It gave me the fabulous power to alter the hormones of anyone I see!

34
00:04:37,925 --> 00:04:43,365
I can change their sex, body temperature, skin color, growth, even their emotions!

35
00:04:43,785 --> 00:04:47,925
I can remodel people from the inside out, like an engineer of the human body!

36
00:04:48,305 --> 00:04:53,325
The candy boys and candy girls you see here have used my help to really kick gender in its sorry pants!

37
00:04:53,745 --> 00:04:55,985
Some men became women and some women men!

38
00:04:56,205 --> 00:04:59,025
But all of those hang-ups are a thing of the past!

39
00:05:00,025 --> 00:05:03,005
In short, those are the kind of miracles we deal in here!

40
00:05:03,165 --> 00:05:04,565
I just provide the hormones!

41
00:05:04,905 --> 00:05:05,345
Ha-ha!

42
00:05:05,585 --> 00:05:07,345
Everyone else provides the dream!

43
00:05:07,345 --> 00:05:08,345
Woo-hoo!

44
00:05:09,125 --> 00:05:10,205
Oh, oh yeah!

45
00:05:11,865 --> 00:05:15,705
He changed that man from earlier into a woman by injecting hormones!

46
00:05:16,345 --> 00:05:16,825
Oh!

47
00:05:25,265 --> 00:05:28,605
I still can't believe that there's a place like this in the middle of a prison!

48
00:05:28,825 --> 00:05:29,925
I must be dreaming!

49
00:05:30,305 --> 00:05:31,365
It's not a dream!

50
00:05:31,585 --> 00:05:32,625
It's a dream land!

51
00:05:32,625 --> 00:05:41,105
All of these candies you see around here were once lost prisoners who made it here by sheer luck, each with their own story!

52
00:05:41,105 --> 00:05:46,505
See, there are hidden entrances to New Kamaland on every floor of Impel Down!

53
00:05:46,625 --> 00:05:48,265
You just have to keep an eye out for them!

54
00:05:48,465 --> 00:05:54,725
There's one at the Bloody Mountain of Needles, one in the Lair of Wild Beasts, one in the Burning Hellfire!

55
00:05:54,725 --> 00:05:56,985
There's even one in the Mortuary!

56
00:05:56,985 --> 00:06:02,565
We use these handy-dandy passages to go wherever we want in this prison to get everything we need!

57
00:06:02,565 --> 00:06:08,885
A paradise hiding in the bowels of hell itself!

58
00:06:09,025 --> 00:06:11,645
Why the jailers would never believe such an absurdity exists!

59
00:06:11,645 --> 00:06:16,645
Despite living in our hidey-hole, we still keep tabs on everything that's going on outside!

60
00:06:17,165 --> 00:06:21,605
We've got a line in one of the transponder snails, the very same ones the jailers use!

61
00:06:22,125 --> 00:06:25,665
That way we're in on all the hip and horrible happenings here in the prison!

62
00:06:26,225 --> 00:06:29,905
We also nab newspapers from the garbage so we can keep up with the other parts of the world!

63
00:06:30,225 --> 00:06:33,465
And we were totally tuning in to Straw Hat Boy's Wild Ride!

64
00:06:33,585 --> 00:06:37,565
It's not every day we get to see them break in, a break out, and all sorts of delectable nonsense!

65
00:06:37,885 --> 00:06:39,545
We were cheering them on the whole way!

66
00:06:39,545 --> 00:06:42,185
But it seems like this place of yours is gigantic!

67
00:06:42,525 --> 00:06:43,745
Where exactly are we?

68
00:06:43,985 --> 00:06:46,305
Oh, this place wasn't always here, I assure you!

69
00:06:46,445 --> 00:06:49,065
Some prisoner had a devil fruit power that was good for digging!

70
00:06:49,385 --> 00:06:51,805
They were the first to start chipping away at these caverns!

71
00:06:52,225 --> 00:06:57,465
They led other prisoners here a long time ago, and bit by bit, the new recruits started building this place together!

72
00:06:58,065 --> 00:07:03,625
To paint a picture, this paradise of ours is actually a bit like an ant farm made from digging tunnels in the rock!

73
00:07:03,945 --> 00:07:09,105
But to answer your question specifically, we are located right in between Level 5 and Level 6!

74
00:07:09,105 --> 00:07:13,325
Whoa! Hang on a minute! Did you say Level 6? I didn't know there was such a thing!

75
00:07:14,825 --> 00:07:18,025
Well, it's not widely known, but I assure you it is there!

76
00:07:18,025 --> 00:07:23,265
Level 6 is where the true villains are kept locked away!

77
00:07:23,625 --> 00:07:27,165
Every one of them is condemned to a lifetime sentence without parole!

78
00:07:27,165 --> 00:07:29,705
It's known as Eternal Hell!

79
00:07:30,705 --> 00:07:33,945
Exceedingly wicked crimes are often covered up by the world government!

80
00:07:34,945 --> 00:07:38,525
As are incidents that would tarnish the reputation of the powers that be!

81
00:07:39,205 --> 00:07:42,705
You know, like your little rampage that took you all the way to Level 4!

82
00:07:42,705 --> 00:07:49,005
If you had tried to pull that same maneuver a little while back, it wouldn't have been so easy, by the way!

83
00:07:49,925 --> 00:07:54,445
There was another beastly baddie guarding this prison not too long ago, you see!

84
00:07:55,225 --> 00:07:59,085
He was the jail manager of Impel Down, Shiryu of the Reign!

85
00:07:59,425 --> 00:08:03,185
And to size him up, he was just as strong as Warden Magellan!

86
00:08:03,185 --> 00:08:07,105
Honestly, considering that Magellan spends most of his time sitting on the crapper,

87
00:08:07,245 --> 00:08:09,365
you might say Shiryu was twice as troublesome!

88
00:08:11,045 --> 00:08:14,145
As strong as the Warden? Is that even possible?

89
00:08:14,725 --> 00:08:19,125
Security's not too shabby these days, but when he was around, it was downright iron tight!

90
00:08:20,905 --> 00:08:24,005
But you said he's gone now? What happened?

91
00:08:33,185 --> 00:08:46,665
You said he's gone now, Shiryu, what do you think you're doing?

92
00:08:47,845 --> 00:08:48,945
My job.

93
00:08:49,325 --> 00:08:54,245
The prisoners aren't here for your amusement. I remind you that we're jailers, not butchers.

94
00:08:55,705 --> 00:08:58,545
No one cares about the lives of these vermin.

95
00:08:58,925 --> 00:09:00,905
I will not tolerate this any longer.

96
00:09:00,905 --> 00:09:04,545
If someone were to find out about half the atrocities you've committed,

97
00:09:04,865 --> 00:09:07,225
Impel Down would be disgraced beyond measure.

98
00:09:07,725 --> 00:09:11,825
Now I must exercise my authority as Warden and place you under arrest.

99
00:09:21,205 --> 00:09:27,285
He killed prisoners when and as he saw fit, even on the slightest whim.

100
00:09:27,285 --> 00:09:32,685
He was completely out of control, so now they hold him in the darkest corners of level six

101
00:09:32,685 --> 00:09:34,365
as a high-security risk.

102
00:09:35,805 --> 00:09:37,885
Unbelievable! I've never heard of this!

103
00:09:38,285 --> 00:09:40,565
I know it happened before I got here, but even so!

104
00:09:40,685 --> 00:09:42,085
He's in fine company, too!

105
00:09:42,465 --> 00:09:45,505
Catalina Davon, the world's most dangerous woman, is down there.

106
00:09:45,865 --> 00:09:48,325
And San Juan Wolf, the great battleship.

107
00:09:48,705 --> 00:09:50,785
Even heavy drinker Vosco Schott!

108
00:09:50,785 --> 00:09:54,485
The names of these criminals are enough to make anyone tremble with fear!

109
00:09:58,685 --> 00:10:01,305
It's the worst of the worst on level six.

110
00:10:02,365 --> 00:10:07,385
Half the crimes these villains committed were so heinous, even the newspapers dared not mention them.

111
00:10:07,925 --> 00:10:09,965
Your former boss is there, too.

112
00:10:10,245 --> 00:10:12,645
I suppose he was pretty wild in his own way.

113
00:10:13,025 --> 00:10:15,765
Mr. Zero? Crocodile?

114
00:10:15,765 --> 00:10:22,085
Um, back in Alabaster, you had quite the little scuffle with Straw Hat Boy, didn't you?

115
00:10:22,825 --> 00:10:24,345
And look at you now.

116
00:10:26,025 --> 00:10:29,905
It just goes to show you that the power of friendship crosses all boundaries.

117
00:10:31,285 --> 00:10:32,225
Reach it, friend!

118
00:10:32,545 --> 00:10:36,565
Oh, and there's one of the warlords down there, the first son of the sea, Gene Ray.

119
00:10:36,905 --> 00:10:37,305
Huh?

120
00:10:37,545 --> 00:10:41,205
Along with that other guy, the one Straw Hat Boy came here to save.

121
00:10:41,205 --> 00:10:46,745
Second Division Commander of the Whitebeard Pirates, the Fire Fist, Portgusty Ace.

122
00:10:47,205 --> 00:10:48,605
I heard about it over the radio.

123
00:10:48,925 --> 00:10:50,525
They're brothers, if I'm not mistaken.

124
00:10:52,725 --> 00:10:53,905
Yes, that's right.

125
00:10:54,185 --> 00:10:56,905
Straw Boy said he only came to Ippel Down to rescue him.

126
00:10:57,985 --> 00:11:01,885
It's insane that he thought to sneak in, and miraculous that he did it.

127
00:11:02,085 --> 00:11:05,005
Um, too bad his plan is dead in the water now.

128
00:11:05,005 --> 00:11:12,865
He has to save himself first, which unfortunately means that he's out of time.

129
00:11:13,205 --> 00:11:16,225
Ace Boy is set to be executed this afternoon at 3 p.m.

130
00:11:16,345 --> 00:11:19,845
I believe they're going to transfer him to Navy Headquarters sometime this morning.

131
00:11:20,465 --> 00:11:26,825
It's already past midnight, so that means Ace Boy will be taken out of Ippel Down in seven or eight hours, tops.

132
00:11:29,505 --> 00:11:33,705
Straw Boy's treatment is going to take two more days to run its course.

133
00:11:33,705 --> 00:11:38,925
And even if he survives, he'll need another three days of recovery to restore his strength.

134
00:11:39,085 --> 00:11:41,465
So by the time he wakes up, it'll all be over.

135
00:11:42,425 --> 00:11:43,505
Are you crazy?

136
00:11:43,825 --> 00:11:45,765
He can't take two more days of that torture.

137
00:11:46,005 --> 00:11:47,105
It's killing him.

138
00:11:47,305 --> 00:11:49,885
As I told you, his chances are extremely low.

139
00:11:49,965 --> 00:11:51,365
We'll need a miracle to make it.

140
00:11:55,805 --> 00:11:57,905
He's not the only one that needs rest.

141
00:11:58,025 --> 00:11:59,365
You had a rough run, too.

142
00:11:59,545 --> 00:12:03,525
Eat something nutritious and go back to bed until you feel like your old self again.

143
00:12:03,705 --> 00:12:06,525
I have a nice, quiet room, just perfect for nappy time.

144
00:12:12,285 --> 00:12:13,165
Screw that!

145
00:12:13,245 --> 00:12:14,505
I'm staying with Straw Boy!

146
00:12:14,585 --> 00:12:15,785
Easy, easy.

147
00:12:16,045 --> 00:12:16,785
There's no need.

148
00:12:16,785 --> 00:12:18,765
There's little hope he'll survive anyway.

149
00:12:19,185 --> 00:12:20,445
It won't do any good.

150
00:12:22,705 --> 00:12:23,145
Oh!

151
00:12:23,145 --> 00:12:37,725
Please, Straw Boy, just...

152
00:12:37,725 --> 00:12:46,565
Hang in there!

153
00:12:46,565 --> 00:12:58,685
I wonder what he's doing back there.

154
00:12:59,525 --> 00:13:01,985
There's not much he can do, is there?

155
00:13:05,985 --> 00:13:07,765
Hang in there!

156
00:13:07,765 --> 00:13:11,285
You can do it, Straw Boy!

157
00:13:13,925 --> 00:13:15,745
I believe in you!

158
00:13:18,805 --> 00:13:20,045
Hang in there!

159
00:13:20,445 --> 00:13:21,745
You can do it!

160
00:13:21,805 --> 00:13:22,985
You've got to be kidding me.

161
00:13:23,065 --> 00:13:24,585
He's been doing that this whole time.

162
00:13:24,885 --> 00:13:25,105
Ha!

163
00:13:25,825 --> 00:13:26,265
Ridiculous!

164
00:13:26,485 --> 00:13:28,445
What's he going to do, yell him back alive?

165
00:13:28,445 --> 00:13:30,025
Come on, let's go.

166
00:13:30,145 --> 00:13:31,365
He'll pass out soon enough.

167
00:13:31,745 --> 00:13:33,125
Hang in there!

168
00:13:40,345 --> 00:13:42,165
Hang in there!

169
00:13:46,785 --> 00:13:48,445
